<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n605" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγκῡρα</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anchor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				18.9
			</span></i> (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγκοινα</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				459
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. βάλλεσθαι, καθιέναι,
				μεθιέναι, ἀΦιέναι</span> to cast <i>anchor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				6(5).13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				662
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				3.5.10
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. αἴρειν, αἴρεσθαι</span>
			to weigh <i>anchor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pomp.</u>
				50
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				80
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέλοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					10.1
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς νέας ἔχειν ἐπ᾽ ἀγκυρέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.12
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρμίζειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.59
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἀγκυρέων ὁρμεῖν</span>
			ride at <i>anchor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.188
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηῦς μιῆς ἐπ̓ ἀγκύρης [ον̓κ ἀσΦ]αλὴς
					ὁρμεῦσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Herod.
					1.41
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ̓ ἀγκύρας ἀποσαλεύειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					50.22
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1071
			</span></i>; prov, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαθαὶ πέλοντ᾽ . . δύ᾽
				ἄγκυραι</span> 'tis good to have 'two strings to your bow',
				<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				6.101
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ δυοῖν ἀγκύραιν ὁρμεῖν αὐτοὺς
					ἐᾶτε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					56.44
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sol.</u>
				19
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. δ᾽ ἥ μου τὰς τύχας ὤχει μόνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					277
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τῆς αὐτῆς</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκύρας</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">
				ὁρμεῖν τοῖς πολλοῖς,</span> i.e. 'to be in the same boat'
			with the many, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.281
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσζ μητρζ παῖδες ἄγκυραι βίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					685
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴκων ἄ.,</span> of a son,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				80
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερὰ ἄ.,</span> last hope,
				<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>JTr.</u>
				51
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>pruning-hook,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				3.2.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰδοῖον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				191
			</span></i>.</div>
